hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"157","Narrated by Muhammad bin Rafi’, narrated by Ishaq bin Issa, who said: I asked Malik about a man who wiped the front of his head during ablution. Does that reward him? He said: Amr bin Yahya bin Amara told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Mazini, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped While performing ablution, he bowed his head from the forelock to the back of it, then returned his hands to the forelock and wiped his entire head.”"
